This implementation handles asynchronous data fetching from multiple external sources by using a `for...of` loop to iterate over each section in the document. It also manages memory efficiently by reusing arrays instead of creating new ones for each section, which helps to minimize unnecessary computational overhead and prevent memory leaks. Additionally, it supports modular design by using an object to store the extracted guidelines, which makes it easier to update or extend the function in the future.

