* `callback`: An optional callback function that takes in a single element as its argument and returns a boolean value indicating whether the element should be included in the result set. If this argument is not provided, all matching elements will be returned.
* `depthLimit`: The maximum depth limit for traversal. If this argument is not provided, the default value of 5 will be used.

The function returns an array of elements that match the given CSS selector and pass the optional callback function if provided. It handles edge cases such as when the root element or selector are invalid, or when the document is not fully loaded. It also prevents infinite loops by checking for self-matching or descendant matching. The function supports a maximum depth limit to mitigate performance issues with deeply nested DOM structures and provides default values for the callback function and depth limit that can be overridden by the caller.

