The trade-off between maintaining high throughput during peak loads and ensuring that the system remains responsive under heavy load is achieved by using a separate thread for event persistence and retrieval, which allows the main application to continue running smoothly while events are being persisted or retrieved. The function is tested thoroughly under stress conditions to validate its robustness and performance characteristics.']

