The linked list and hash table are protected by a mutex lock to ensure concurrent access to shared resources is handled safely and efficiently. The linked list is implemented as a singly-linked list, with each node storing a pointer to the next node in the list. The hash table is implemented as an array of buckets, with each bucket containing a linked list of nodes that have the same hash code.

