The code uses memory pools to reduce fragmentation and improve cache locality by allocating the arrays in large chunks and dividing them among the processors. It also design the data structures to facilitate quick insertion and retrieval operations, balancing between memory usage and access speed.

Finally, the code is scalable to accommodate a growing number of processors and data points without significant performance degradation by using a linked list for managing the collection of processors."]

