The `init_logging_system` function initializes the logging system context by allocating memory for the arrays and initializing the linked list head. It also initializes the mutex used to protect the linked list.

The `add_log_entry` function adds a new log entry to the linked list. It first allocates memory for the new node and then adds it to the linked list. The function also updates the timestamp of the log entry to the current system time.

The `remove_log_entry` function removes a log entry from the linked list. It searches for the specified message in the linked list and then removes the corresponding node.

The `traverse_log_entries` function traverses the linked list and prints all log entries.

The `release_logging_system` function releases memory for the linked list and arrays. It also unlocks the mutex used to protect the linked list.

This code is optimized for performance by carefully managing cache usage and reducing false sharing in multi-threaded environments. It also includes a mechanism to automatically recover from transient errors, such as network failures or connection issues with external databases.']

