This code also includes a mechanism to efficiently update or delete records, considering the trade-offs between write-throughput and read-latency, and an implementation of a write-back cache to reduce immediate writes to shared memory, ensuring minimal impact on overall system performance. Additionally, the system is designed to support periodic data pruning to remove outdated entries, balancing performance and memory optimization, and accounting for the potential variability in data arrival rates and access patterns.']

