The `traverse` function traverses the tree and prints both the keys and their corresponding metadata timestamps.

To handle the real-world constraints of limited system memory, frequent insertions and deletions, and concurrent access from multiple threads, this implementation uses a mutex to ensure thread safety when modifying the tree structure. It also uses a reference count for each node to track usage frequency and delete nodes that are no longer used.

To optimize performance for read-heavy operations while ensuring efficient memory utilization, this implementation uses a vector of nodes to store the keys and their corresponding metadata timestamps during traversal. This allows for minimal impact on system performance while minimizing memory fragmentation.

