The record array is initialized with an initial capacity and can be resized automatically to accommodate additional records. The hash table is also initialized with an appropriate size and number of elements, and the deque is initialized with an appropriate capacity and number of elements. The system includes a mechanism for handling memory allocation failures and periodically reclaiming unused memory.

The system provides robust core functionalities for adding, removing, updating, and iterating over log entries, ensuring low-latency and efficient resource usage. The system also manages asynchronous external logging services and handles network failures that might affect log data availability. The design of the system is modular and extensible, allowing for future integration with features such as filtering or indexing based on various criteria.

The performance implications of memory access patterns on cache performance are carefully considered in the design of the data structures. The system minimizes cache misses by using a custom deque data structure that supports rapid insertions and deletions from both ends of the buffer, while also minimizing memory usage under high-load conditions.

